  "name": "rainy-window",
  "vibe": "Let it pour. Slate #2c3440 glass with seven bokeh discs breathing in amber #f2b552, blue #7ac7e0 and rose, twelve drops falling at 180–420px/s as streaks with fat heads, and two long condensation runnels wandering the full height of the frame on wobbling control points. Merriweather sets headlines with real italics over Public Sans; the feature card is a #39424f glass panel with a paper hairline. It owns Ring:ring — a 240px circular gauge with twelve tick marks counting a number up — alongside Typing:typewriter, Scroll:feed and Notify:drop. Everything is slow on purpose: drowse titles, 0.4 rotation, 5px drift, the softest camera in this batch. Best for cosy retail, reading and journaling apps, tea and coffee, weather and insurance — anything selling staying in.",
